course: dictionary
lesson: 4273
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning an author wants by reading the words around it. «Greasy» is a good example: it can describe hands, food, hair, or a slippery floor.
explain: Look at «greasy hands» and «greasy chips». The first means covered in oil; the second means cooked with a lot of fat. The words next to greasy are the clue.
explain: Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning in place of the hard word and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Greasy means covered with grease or oil, or full of it.
fact: Food that is greasy has been cooked with a lot of fat or oil, such as «greasy chips».
fact: Hair or skin that looks oily can also be called greasy.
fact: A greasy floor is slippery, so walk carefully on it.
fact: Water alone does not remove oil, so greasy dishes need hot water and soap.
exercise: «Wash the greasy dishes in hot water and soap.» What does greasy mean here? | Sunny and warm | Loud and noisy | Very old | *Covered with oil or fat
exercise: «Mind the greasy floor, it is slippery.» What does greasy suggest? | Clean and dry | Very tall | *Slippery because of oil | Full of toys
exercise: «Butterworts have flat, greasy-looking sticky leaves that catch tiny flies.» What does greasy-looking mean? | Looking very happy | Looking very old | Looking like a bird | *Looking oily
test: «The chips were greasy, so Mia ate a salad instead.» What does greasy mean in this sentence? | *Cooked with a lot of fat or oil | Covered in dust | Cold and wet | Freshly washed
test: In «great grey-green, greasy Limpopo River», what do the words grey-green and greasy share? | They are both colours | They are both kinds of food | They mean exactly the same thing | *The same starting sound
exam: Which sentence uses greasy to mean slippery? | My greasy hair needs a wash. | *The greasy path made her slip. | The greasy chips were tasty. | Wash your greasy dishes with soap.
